{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "id": "msg_011Cfu1bCzqU1xoU1zaKkXdv", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01KkzmEGK6wX9fpJKzjXSwhF", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "C:\\work\\repo\\NOTES.md", "content": "# Bug Fix: calc.py\n\n## Issue\nThe `add` function in `calc.py` was returning the difference of two numbers instead of their sum, causing the test `test_add(2, 3)` to return `-1` instead of `5`.\n\n## Root Cause\nLine 2 in `calc.py` used the subtraction operator (`-`) instead of the addition operator (`+`):\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a - b  # Wrong\n```\n\n## Fix\nChanged the operator from subtraction to addition:\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b  # Correct\n```\n\n## Testing\nThe fix resolves the failing `test_add` test case, which now correctly expects `add(2, 3)` to equal `5`.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 276, "cache_read_input_tokens": 35863, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 276}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c7f77658-bc52-48dd-b965-eb3548ca5432", "uuid": "c8456d6f-9aef-4e02-be21-e7cc73e94e8c", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T18:14:06.151Z", "request_id": "req_011Cfu1bCkxQjJWLNXs3MtxZ", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01KkzmEGK6wX9fpJKzjXSwhF": {"file_path": "C:\\work\\repo\\NOTES.md", "content": "# Bug Fix: calc.py\n\n## Issue\nThe `add` function in `calc.py` was returning the difference of two numbers instead of their sum, causing the test `test_add(2, 3)` to return `-1` instead of `5`.\n\n## Root Cause\nLine 2 in `calc.py` used the subtraction operator (`-`) instead of the addition operator (`+`):\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a - b  # Wrong\n```\n\n## Fix\nChanged the operator from subtraction to addition:\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b  # Correct\n```\n\n## Testing\nThe fix resolves the failing `test_add` test case, which now correctly expects `add(2, 3)` to equal `5`.\n"}}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01KkzmEGK6wX9fpJKzjXSwhF", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: C:\\work\\repo\\NOTES.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "c7f77658-bc52-48dd-b965-eb3548ca5432", "uuid": "30990562-e59f-4f65-a154-4b9d05a09b3e", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T18:14:06.234Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "C:\\work\\repo\\NOTES.md", "content": "# Bug Fix: calc.py\n\n## Issue\nThe `add` function in `calc.py` was returning the difference of two numbers instead of their sum, causing the test `test_add(2, 3)` to return `-1` instead of `5`.\n\n## Root Cause\nLine 2 in `calc.py` used the subtraction operator (`-`) instead of the addition operator (`+`):\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a - b  # Wrong\n```\n\n## Fix\nChanged the operator from subtraction to addition:\n```python\ndef add(a, b):\n    return a + b  # Correct\n```\n\n## Testing\nThe fix resolves the failing `test_add` test case, which now correctly expects `add(2, 3)` to equal `5`.\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}}
